course: dictionary
lesson: 6875
title: Overlap: the part shared
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To overlap means to cover part of the same space as something else, so one thing lies partly over another. It can also mean two things happen partly at the same time. An overlap is the part that is shared or covered twice.
explain: «Draw two overlapping circles.» The circles share a patch in the middle. That shared patch is the overlap, and anything inside it belongs to both circles.
explain: «If the player overlaps a wall, the game pushes the player back.» Here the player and the wall would take up the same space, which is not allowed, so the game pushes the player out. The context tells you that overlap means sharing space.
explain: «Bricks that overlap the joins, like a real brick wall, make a much stronger tower than bricks stacked straight up.» Overlapping bricks cover the join below them, so the wall holds together. Stacked straight up, they can snap.
fact: Overlap can be a verb (to overlap) or a noun (an overlap).
fact: «Overlapping» means lying partly over something else.
fact: In a Venn diagram, the overlap holds the things that are in both groups.
fact: Roof tiles and fish scales overlap to keep water out.
fact: The pangolin is covered in hard overlapping scales made of keratin, like fingernails.
exercise: «Draw two overlapping circles.» What does overlapping mean here? | Spinning very fast | Lying far apart with empty space between | Drawn in red | *Lying partly over each other, sharing a patch
exercise: In a Venn diagram, what does the overlap hold? | Only the biggest numbers | *Things that are in both groups | Things in neither group | Nothing at all
exercise: «Bricks that overlap the joins make a much stronger tower.» What makes this tower stronger? | Fewer bricks | Bricks stacked straight up | Smaller bricks | *Bricks overlapping the joins
test: Roof tiles overlap. Why? | *To keep water out | To hide the sky | To make a noise in the rain | To make the roof heavier for no reason
test: Which sentence uses overlap to mean happening partly at the same time? | *The swimming club and the choir overlap on Tuesdays | The bus stopped at the corner | The cat sat on the mat | The bread is in the oven
exam: Ella says an overlap is a gap between two things. Is she right? | Yes, because gaps and overlaps are the same | No, overlaps only happen in music | *No, an overlap is the part shared or covered twice | Yes, an overlap is always empty space
